# zp configuration

Nested. Generated by cfgx from the schema; don't edit.

Each setting comes from, highest first: a flag, an environment variable, the config file (`config.yaml`, `.yml` or `.json`, looked for in `.`, `$HOME/.zp`, or named by `--config` or `ZP_CONFIG`), or its default. An empty value counts as not set.

## `database`

Database connection.

| Key | Description | Type | Default | Env | Flag | Used by |
|-----|-------------|------|---------|-----|------|---------|
| `database.host` | Host. Deprecated: use host instead. Formerly `database.hostname`. | string |  | `ZP_DATABASE_HOST` | `--database-host` | Serve |

## `server`

HTTP server.

| Key | Description | Type | Default | Env | Flag | Used by |
|-----|-------------|------|---------|-----|------|---------|
| `server.port` | Port. | int | `7777` | `ZP_SERVER_PORT` | `--port` | Serve |
| `server.tls.enabled` | Serve HTTPS. | bool |  | `ZP_SERVER_TLS_ENABLED` | `--tls-enabled` | Serve |
| `server.tls.cert` | TLS certificate. | string | `cert.pem` | `ZP_SERVER_TLS_CERT` | `--tls-cert` | Serve |

